.TH EUCLID-CLI-EQS-LIST-QUEUES 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eqs-list-queues \- list queues
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eqs list-queues
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR|\fB\-p\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR|\fB\-i\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-column\fR|\fB\-c\fR \fICOLUMN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists queues, optionally filtered by name prefix and paginated.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Only list queues whose name starts with this prefix. Optional; if
omitted, all queues are listed.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of queues to return. Defaults to \fI-1\fR (no paging).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-page\-index " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page index to return when \fB\-\-page\-size\fR is set.
Defaults to \fI-1\fR.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-sort\-column " " \fICOLUMN\fR
Column to sort results by. Defaults to \fIname\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The matching queues are printed as JSON (possibly an empty list).
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or the
server rejected the request.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs list-queues

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs list-queues \e
    --prefix orders- --page-size 20 --page-index 0 --sort-column name
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-create-queue (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-get-queue-ern (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-get-queue-metadata (1)
